   43                                   ; The changes include:
   44                                   ;   - Fixed up indentation.
   45                                   ;   - Added comments and routine headers.
   46                                   ;
   47                                   ; The home of this file and the rest of the Tempest 2000 source code is:
   48                                   ;    https://github.com/mwenge/tempest2k 
   49                                   ;             
   50                                   ; Objects in Tempest 2000
   51                                   ; -----------------------
   52                                   ; Nearly every game element in Tempest 2000 is an 'object' that is managed
   53                                   ; in the list of all active game objects called 'activeobjects'. Each object
   54                                   ; is 64 bytes of data and represents the total state of that object, including
   55                                   ; its position, behaviour, the routine to use for drawing it, and the routine
   56                                   ; to use for updating it.


                                        src/yak.s            Page 2       5:01:00 pm 29-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.1.01 (Linux/OSX)


   57                                   ;
   58                                   ; As enemies are created and killed they are moved in and out of the activeobjects
   59                                   ; list. Likewise for the player's claw and all the bullets the enemies and the player
   60                                   ; fire at each other. Once every frame, we need to take the state of all these objects and draw
   61                                   ; them on the screen. While the state of every object is updated in the 'Frame'
   62                                   ; routine, they are drawn to the screen by draw_objects in the game's 'mainloop'. 
   63                                   ; 'Drawing' here means using the GPU or the Blitter to convert each object's state
   64                                   ; into some pixel data and including that data in a block of data that represents
   65                                   ; either the whole or part of the screen displayed to the player.
   66                                   ;
   67                                   ; The structure for all members in the activeobjects list is broadly as follows:
   68                                   ;
   69                                   ;  -----    ---------------------------------------------------------------
   70                                   ;  Table 1: The structure of an 'activobject' in Tempest 2000.
   71                                   ;  Bytes    Solid Objects                                    
   72                                   ;  -----    -------------------------------------------------
   73                                   ;  0-3      Index into draw routine in 'solids'.             
   74                                   ;  4-7      X 
   75                                   ;  8-11     Y 
   76                                   ;  12-15    Z 
   77                                   ;  16-19    Position/lane on web.
   78                                   ;  20-23    Velocity 
   79                                   ;  24-27    Acceleration/Flipper Mode                        
   80                                   ;  28-29    XZ Orientation  (Roll)                           
   81                                   ;  30-31    Y Rotation  (Pitch)
   82                                   ;  32-33    Z Rotation  (Yaw)
   83                                   ;  34-35    Draw Type (Index into draw routine in draw_vex)
   84                                   ;  36-39    Start address of pixel data.                     
   85                                   ;  40-41    Colour 
   86                                   ;  42-43    Scale factor 
   87                                   ;  44-45    0 = climb rail, 1 = cross rail, 2 = blowaway
   88                                   ;  46-49    Size of Pixel Data/Number of pixels/Duration/Secondary Object Update Routine
   89                                   ;  50-51    Marked for deletion 
   90                                   ;  52-53    0 = not an enemy, 1 = enemy, -1 = vulnerable
   91                                   ;  54-55    Object Type  (Index into update routine in run_vex).
   92                                   ;  56-59    Address of Previous Object 
   93                                   ;  60-63    Address of Next Object 
   94                                   ;
   95                                   ;  -----    ---------------------------------------------------------------
   96                                   ;  Table 1: The structure of an 'activobject' in Tempest 2000.
   97                                   ;  Bytes    Solid Objects                                    
   98                                   ;  -----    -------------------------------------------------
   99                                   ;  0-3      Index into draw routine in 'solids'.             
  100                                   ;  4-7      X 
  101                                   ;  8-11     Y 
  102                                   ;  12-15    Z 
  103                                   ;  16-19    Position/lane on web.
  104                                   ;  20-23    Velocity 
